# HemaMatch environment variables (Vite)
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values for YOUR project.
#
#   Supabase : Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
#                - Project URL          -> VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#                - anon / public key    -> VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   Cloudinary: Dashboard home -> Cloud name; Settings -> Upload ->
#               Add upload preset (Signing Mode: UNSIGNED) -> preset name
#
# The app runs in MOCK MODE until the Supabase variables are filled in,
# so you can develop and demo with zero setup. See README for details.

# --- Supabase (Phase 2) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# --- Cloudinary (v3: profile photo uploads) ---
# OPTIONAL: without these the Profile page offers a "paste an image URL"
# fallback instead, so the demo still works.
# Free account at https://cloudinary.com -> create an UNSIGNED upload
# preset (Settings -> Upload -> "Add upload preset" -> Signing Mode:
# UNSIGNED) -> copy the preset name here.
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your-cloud-name
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=your-unsigned-preset-name

# --- Mode switch (optional) ---
# Leave unset for automatic behavior:
#   - Supabase env vars present -> Supabase mode
#   - missing                   -> mock mode (localStorage)
# Set to "true" to force mock mode, "false" to force Supabase mode:
# VITE_USE_MOCK=true

# --- SECURITY (read this before your defense) ---
# Only VITE_ variables reach the browser, and the two Supabase values are
# public BY DESIGN — authorization is enforced by Row Level Security in
# PostgreSQL, not by hiding the key. The service_role key must NEVER be
# placed in this file or in any frontend code: it bypasses RLS entirely.
# The Cloudinary preset is UNSIGNED on purpose: it can only upload
# images, and your Cloudinary settings control formats/folders — there
# is no API secret in the browser. If you ever leak a secret, rotate it
# immediately.
